WEBVTT

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:05.890
I've never seen this building before.

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:09.180
But it must be my apartment building.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.100
Because my wife is here.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:21.100
My wife is laughing.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.850
Back then we didn't even need a reason to laugh.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:31.310
Hey, Dad, you've made outstanding
contributions at work several times, right?

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:34.890
Do you think you were just
cut out to be a police officer?

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:37.810
Well, I think I might have been lucky.

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.270
Can't really say if I'm cut out for it.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:42.100
Lucky, huh?

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.140
Hey, do you think I'm cut out to be an officer?

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:47.970
Hmm.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.270
No such conversation happened.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:54.850
From the moment I became a homicide
detective, I was always busy with work.

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:58.390
So I think Muku wouldn't have
wanted to be an officer either.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:02.850
And I was never cut out to be on the force.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.970
I couldn't even protect my own family.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:15.560
She and the killer had a fistfight.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:18.470
She must have fought back bravely.

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:19.970
She's beautiful.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:22.390
It didn't look like this.

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:24.520
She had nearly all her bones broken,

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:28.140
her lungs, liver, spleen, and heart demolished,

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:31.810
and half her brain splattered out of her skull.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:34.560
That's how my daughter died.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:40.060
A serial killer called the Challenger
forced her to fight injured head to toe,

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:42.770
she suffered excruciating agony,

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:44.520
and then she was murdered.

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.600
Come in.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.520
How are you feeling?

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:22.850
Good to see you.

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.350
I still get light-headed and dizzy.

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:29.520
Oh, but today's been going well.
And my rehab is proceeding smoothly.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:34.140
Good. Take it slow.
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:37.560
Mr. Matsuoka, I have a question
about the Perforator case.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.100
What the hell did I just tell you?

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.680
The Mizuhanome created
an id well from me, right?

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.970
What was it like?

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:48.520
It's better you not know.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.930
Sakaido entered it, didn't he?

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:55.100
Lucky. I wish I could.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:56.470
You can't.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:59.560
Entering your own id well is prohibited.

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:03.220
Your well comes from your unconscious.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:06.930
To dive into it is to become
conscious of the unconscious.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:08.810
Ultimately this is all theoretical,

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:11.970
but in an attempt to avoid
the consciousness's invasion,

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:15.470
the id well would render
itself invisible and expand.

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:17.520
Like a rising storm.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.970
Then the storm swallows the brilliant detective,

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:24.140
who winds up wandering
in their own well forever.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:26.930
Apparently, they "fall into dogma."

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:30.350
Dogma... What's supposed to mean?

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:31.810
Hell if I know.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:34.680
Anyway, they say the
pilot's location data is lost,

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.430
and pilot retrieval becomes impossible.

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:39.310
The pilot doesn't just die?

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:44.390
The body in the cockpit might struggle
to maintain its functions at some point.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.060
However, even if the body dies,

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:48.930
the mind apparently lives
on inside the Mizuhanome.

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:50.310
Oh.

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:53.430
The pilot losing their memories inside the well

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:57.310
and becoming the brilliant detective
is probably a safety feature

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:59.520
in case the pilot enters their own well.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:00.720
Are you listening?

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:04.100
Huh? Oh, uh, you must be right.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:10.180
To think other people are looking at
a part of my mind that I don't know

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:12.310
and going in and out of it...

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:13.890
How fun.

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:17.640
Where's your mother?

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:20.100
Seems like she's not here today.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:23.770
My mom's not all that interested in me.

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:26.520
Hey now.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:29.470
You're going to catch the Pyrotechnician, right?

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:32.390
Lucky. I wish I could participate.

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:35.140
You barely got out of the last operation alive.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:36.350
Aren't you scared?

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:40.390
Hmm. I'm not really scared.

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:45.520
It's hard to describe,
but it's more like I'm angry.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:50.060
Not just at the Perforator--
I mean Tamotsu Fukuda.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.930
At all serial killers.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:58.560
Oh, I did lose a little bit of my frontal lobe,

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:02.390
but there's no damage to the
limbic system, which is farther back.

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:05.930
So there should be no effect
on say, anger or pleasure.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:08.600
Anger and pleasure, huh?

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:11.560
You might be a little like Narihisago.

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:14.310
Like Sakaido?! The brilliant detective!

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:17.600
Not the brilliant detective, the real-world pilot.

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:22.520
He didn't say it in so many
words, but that happened to him.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:25.470
Like an odd combination of pleasure and anger.

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:30.430
Oh, yeah. You and
Narihisago were colleagues.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.680
Hmm, I see.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.850
Could <i>I </i>be a brilliant detective?

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:37.600
You formed a well, so you're probably eligible.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:41.140
But having that talent
is a question of capabilities.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.770
Hmm, capabilities.

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:47.600
That depends on how much of a boost
the Mizuhanome's adjustments provide.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:49.560
Give up on this.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:53.470
Becoming a pilot is tantamount to suicide.

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:59.520
Thankfully you survived your first one.
No need to attempt a second.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:04.060
You're... worrying about me, right?

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:09.390
I didn't care much for Narihisago
when we were both detectives.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:15.060
And now I truly disdain him as hopeless trash.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:16.600
Anyway, just rest.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:19.100
Leave this guy to us.

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:24.180
I'll let you in on one bit of good news.

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:27.310
The cognition particles
weren't blown away this time.

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:29.850
We found some at the scene.

00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:31.520
No mistake about it.

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:35.060
We gleaned them from the remnants
of some unexploded gunpowder.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:36.770
They're the Pyrotechnician's.

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:39.180
I authorize construction of a well.

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:40.350
Roger.

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:42.270
Go call Narihisago.

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:46.350
Hey there...

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.180
Where are <i>you </i>going?

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:20.140
Where am I?

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:36.350
I remember.

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:39.220
Her name is Kaeru.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:44.850
And, by remembering her,
I remember who I am, too.

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:48.060
My name is Sakaido--the brilliant detective.

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:51.770
I don't know my full name,
but that's not important right now.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:55.600
I must solve the mystery of Kaeru's death.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:56.850
What is this?

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:58.930
What's going on?

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:00.270
A sniper?

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:03.930
Hey, don't just stand there!

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:05.470
Hurry up and hide!

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:08.680
What are you doing?

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:09.720
You have to hide!

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:13.810
Whatever. Just stand there and die, then.

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:15.600
Oh, yeah, I might die.

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.310
Can't have that, can I?

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:21.890
The shooting stopped.

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:25.060
Is it because everyone hid behind the wall?

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:28.140
A blind spot means there's only one sniper.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.350
Where?

00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:32.720
It appears the bullets are
coming from inside the waterfall,

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:36.560
but the water is obscuring
everything, even the muzzle flash.

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:39.350
The water on the ground washes away the blood,

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:41.270
so I can't trace the trajectory.

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:43.270
I can't locate the sniper.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:46.060
That's fine. Focus on observation.

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:49.520
Dammit!

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:51.430
I didn't come here to die.

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:54.890
But my job is not survival.

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:59.720
What I'm supposed to do is solve
the mystery of Kaeru's death.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:01.390
Something's wrong here.

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:04.640
But what? I'm not really sure.

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.890
"Something's wrong"? What is it?

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:10.520
A total of 75 people are on the tower.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.060
None have been recognized.

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:14.020
This seems not to be a real place.

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:16.270
The time can only be narrowed to midday.

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:19.850
Habutae, I believe identifying
anyone will prove impossible.

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:21.060
Look.

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:27.270
Oh, that's why. They're no one,
and it doesn't matter who they are.

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:29.310
Are they just generic "others"?

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:34.560
They're something like dolls produced
from a mix of different people's features.

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:37.470
Seems fitting of our indiscriminate killer.

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:41.270
The clothing is also slapdash.
No brands can be determined.

00:09:41.270 --> 00:09:45.430
Not a problem. We'll keep
identifying what we can't determine.

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:48.140
People tend to hide things unconsciously.

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:50.560
If the Pyrotechnician is meticulous,

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:53.270
they might hide things meticulously as well.

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:58.720
They made bombs and arranged gunpowder
and fireworks to create pleasing displays.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:00.770
That's meticulous work.

00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:05.720
Good point. I had been imagining
more of an attention seeker.

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:09.810
What is causing this feeling?

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:12.390
Extract Sakaido!

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:22.350
Re-inject Sakaido.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.350
--Ready?
--Of course.

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:39.390
My name is Sakaido.

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:40.560
Extraction!

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:42.970
What feels wrong about Kaeru's body?

00:10:54.470 --> 00:10:56.640
The repositioning is too fast.

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:59.220
Are there multiple snipers after all?

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:03.020
Why do we have to be killed?!

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:04.890
That I do not know.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:08.430
But if this is a senseless
slaughter to the victims,

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.970
then there might not be a reason.

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:15.270
The number of victims excluding
Kaeru and Sakaido changes each time.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:18.270
So far, it's between 71 and 83.

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:20.100
Continue analyzing.

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:26.770
I can't take it anymore!
Anything's better than getting shot!

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:29.770
I can't stay here!

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:32.350
Don't shoot me!

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:42.640
Is it better to be shot, or to jump?

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:44.890
Don't stop moving!

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:53.850
Dammit! Dammit!

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:59.810
Compared to staying put, how much
difference will all that effort make?

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:04.060
Either way, death will come to you.

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:08.770
Remember though, my
purpose here is not to survive.

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:11.350
Don't be afraid.

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:12.810
I am a brilliant detective.

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:15.770
My purpose is to solve the
mystery of Kaeru's death.

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:19.640
Please help me! Please! Do something!

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:21.100
Hey, wait!

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:23.180
Something about Kaeru's body!

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:26.270
Come on, self. Think! Look closely!

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:31.470
What is it? What's wrong with this picture?

00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:35.220
I can't take it anymore!
I don't want to die this way!

00:12:35.220 --> 00:12:39.140
Go ahead. At least it will be a little quieter.

00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:48.180
Stop! Let go!

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:50.640
Sorry. Couldn't help it.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:56.100
I can't take this! I just need it all to stop!

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:59.020
Hmm. It pays to get involved.

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:01.180
Mystery solved.

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:02.350
Wait, what?

00:13:02.350 --> 00:13:07.470
Oh, of course! We couldn't tell
because the sun is directly overhead!

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:10.350
Oh, you can't tell if you're always moving.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:14.220
Hey, come on, now! You're making me look bad!

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:28.220
The guy who jumped from the other
side earlier is directly below me now.

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:30.350
How would that happen?

00:13:39.140 --> 00:13:41.970
The tower is what's moving.

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:45.220
That's how the sniper repositioned so quickly.

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:48.310
Or rather, how it looked that way.

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:55.560
It started off with rapid fire,
but the aim was precise.

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:58.470
You can't accomplish such a feat while moving.

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:03.060
The sniper must have been sniping us
from the same spot as we ran around.

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:04.970
What happened was this:

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:09.100
Kaeru was shot in the chest.

00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:10.850
She went down,

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:15.310
but she was still conscious
and spotted the sniper.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:20.810
To help the rest of us,
she indicated the direction.

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:23.180
The tower was moving then, too,

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:26.890
so her finger deviated from
the trajectory of the bullet.

00:14:29.140 --> 00:14:32.520
That deviation is what made
things look wrong to me.

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:45.060
Oh, what's this? Still alive?

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:51.180
Everyone, run randomly
so you're harder to target!

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:55.930
I see. So only you proceed at a steady pace.

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:04.520
Don't give up! Find the sniper!

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:05.930
Don't die!

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:08.310
He seems to be enjoying himself.

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:17.520
The sniper wasn't even moving.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:19.180
Everyone, stay alive!

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:21.680
Just keep running!

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:28.810
What happens when this guy
is the last man standing?

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:34.100
Is another group just brought up
from below for the slaughter?

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:35.810
Oh, you figured me out?

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:38.390
Yeah. I <i>am </i>a brilliant detective.

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:41.560
But you've held your head up a bit too high.

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:43.680
It's fine.

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:46.180
Life and death aren't the issue.

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:55.430
Extract Sakaido!

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:56.680
The puzzle is solved!

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:58.600
Of the 75 victims this time,

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:02.390
74 had their faces and body parts
broken down and randomly reassembled.

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:05.100
Those 74 people were... soldiers.

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:08.390
Victims of a bombing in
the Middle East four years ago.

00:16:11.060 --> 00:16:13.470
It's a political alert.

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:17.430
What do we do? There are
ways to obtain the information.

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:18.720
Leave it.

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:22.140
It'd be used as a political pretext against us.

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:24.930
They'd love to learn the
secrets behind the Mizuhanome,

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:27.680
but we operate the thing and even we don't know.

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:30.770
You said 74 out of 75. What about the last one?

00:16:30.770 --> 00:16:32.060
My apologies, sir.

00:16:32.060 --> 00:16:35.100
The last one is the man Sakaido found.

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:36.680
He's the Pyrotechnician.

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:39.060
He's also had his face changed, though.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:43.180
Plastic surgery. Cross-reference
with all plastic surgery records.

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:44.020
Yes, ma'am!

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:46.180
There's one more thing.

00:16:46.180 --> 00:16:50.850
In the well, the killer was
at the scene of the massacre.

00:16:50.850 --> 00:16:53.100
Could the Pyrotechnician be a soldier?

00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:55.970
Suppose he was also at
the scene of the bombing...

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:57.100
A firefighter?

00:16:57.100 --> 00:16:58.060
Police?

00:16:58.060 --> 00:17:01.680
Or possibly he was among the
crowd of onlookers. So maybe...

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:05.520
Pretended to be a freelance
news photographer at the scene, huh?

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:06.640
Suspect captured.

00:17:06.640 --> 00:17:08.470
Good. Bring him to me.

00:17:10.220 --> 00:17:14.520
Seven procedures in four years makes for quite a difference in appearance.

00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:17.100
Well, but now you get to be handsome.

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:19.600
I don't care how I look.

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:24.930
But saying that to a plastic surgeon
would only raise unnecessary suspicion.

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:26.600
Oh, I see.

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:31.850
Mr. Matsuoka, the photographs you wanted.

00:17:31.850 --> 00:17:37.270
Thanks, I was wondering how clean his
shots of his own firework bombs would be.

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:46.140
The people in this world are
dead long before I kill them.

00:17:48.930 --> 00:17:51.640
You like that photograph that much?

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:56.390
It's not a matter of liking it. It's just real.

00:17:56.390 --> 00:17:58.020
I suppose.

00:17:58.020 --> 00:18:03.310
All humans do love beautiful
things, even if they're terrifying.

00:18:03.310 --> 00:18:08.270
It captures the empty soul of modern man.

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:11.180
"Empty" is an exaggeration, don't you think?

00:18:11.180 --> 00:18:13.850
They witnessed something incredible.

00:18:13.850 --> 00:18:17.310
They're just trying to record it,
or trying to show it to others.

00:18:17.310 --> 00:18:19.680
That's what gawkers do, isn't it?

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:23.180
They're lacking in empathy.

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:30.100
People only died because of <i>your </i>bombs.
Isn't that right... Mr. Pyrotechnician?

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:33.890
I just exposed the emptiness of modern humanity.

00:18:33.890 --> 00:18:35.180
Everyone is insignificant.

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:39.770
It doesn't matter whether anyone
is alive or dead. You included.

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:42.470
Doesn't matter if you're alive or dead.

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:44.220
Well, true.

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:47.890
There's no value in a person's life or death.

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:49.310
You think I'm wrong?

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:52.470
I just don't think you believe that deep down.

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:56.430
I believe it at my core. I know it!

00:18:56.430 --> 00:18:58.270
People's lives have no value.

00:18:58.270 --> 00:19:02.270
Not mine, not yours, and
not your dear daughter's either.

00:19:02.270 --> 00:19:06.020
Whether someone is alive or
dead, either way it's meaningless.

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:12.850
People die... all on their own.

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:15.810
They die of old age. They die of disease.
They die in accidents.

00:19:15.810 --> 00:19:20.350
But the death you brought
about was always mass murder.

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:23.140
Unless a bunch of people die--
unless it's a massacre,

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:27.180
to you it just doesn't count as death.

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:29.100
What are--

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:35.350
Was that bombing four years ago really so magnificent?

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:48.100
That hell struck your fancy.

00:19:48.100 --> 00:19:51.310
A gawker just enjoys the scene.

00:19:51.310 --> 00:19:54.970
But you wanted to savor that hell again so badly

00:19:54.970 --> 00:19:58.220
that you've been recreating it,
over and over and over.

00:19:58.220 --> 00:20:02.060
You bask at the center of your
handmade hell, and you're ecstatic.

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:04.140
That's who you are.

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:05.850
You're wrong!

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:08.930
--I expose reality--
--I'm <i>not </i>wrong.

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:12.770
Your photographs certainly
capture part of reality in this world.

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:15.430
But it's <i>your </i>reality.

00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:17.680
Shallow humans.

00:20:17.680 --> 00:20:20.850
But the shallowness is your own.

00:20:20.850 --> 00:20:21.850
You don't know me!

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:27.350
Tell me. Between setting off the bomb
and taking photos of the onlookers,

00:20:27.350 --> 00:20:28.810
or perhaps while taking the photos,

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:33.470
what were you looking at
as you snapped the camera?

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:38.020
You weren't just gazing upon the gawkers.

00:20:38.020 --> 00:20:42.600
You were stunned and moved by the dreadful beauty of hell, weren't you?

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:51.390
That's ridiculous.

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:54.850
You can't convince me otherwise with your words.

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:57.140
I know it.

00:20:57.140 --> 00:20:59.140
You're mistaken.

00:20:59.140 --> 00:21:02.810
Doesn't matter if you're alive or dead, right?

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:07.600
But the truth is that you want other people to die

00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:10.680
so you can gaze upon them as
the last man standing, don't you?

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:11.640
No!

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:16.970
I already told you. I <i>know </i>my words are true.

00:21:16.970 --> 00:21:21.220
Your words won't reach me anymore.

00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:26.270
You know, your fun is all over now.

00:21:26.270 --> 00:21:28.770
You'll never see hell again.

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:32.560
Except for in your memories.

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:36.890
Haven't you had enough?

00:21:42.770 --> 00:21:47.350
That's right. It's all the same
whether you're alive or dead.

00:21:47.350 --> 00:21:49.720
That's what that means.

00:21:49.720 --> 00:21:51.220
Don't give up.

00:21:51.220 --> 00:21:55.930
Just a little longer and
you'll prove your worldview.

00:22:12.180 --> 00:22:13.430
Get down!

00:22:15.720 --> 00:22:17.020
Kaeru!

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:20.180
I meant to save you.

00:22:20.180 --> 00:22:21.810
I know.

00:22:21.810 --> 00:22:25.430
It's why you've come here so many times.

00:22:25.430 --> 00:22:29.930
I had to. There seemed to be time
before the first shot would kill you.

00:22:31.310 --> 00:22:34.850
The investigation didn't matter to you.

00:22:34.850 --> 00:22:37.930
If your job didn't matter to you to begin with,

00:22:37.930 --> 00:22:42.100
why weren't you with us before we died?

00:22:50.600 --> 00:22:53.180
Everyone up!

00:23:05.100 --> 00:23:08.020
Kaeru isn't Muku.
